From 034084ba28634a31e07461fca07f4ee2892aeacb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app_event): a left may name the screen it went to,
 counted per place

paulgsc/some-ui#3367, the owner's answer: yes. The engagement event's `left` may carry
`next`, the id of the screen it went to: another of its places, `<affordance>.<place>`
of its pipeline, or `elsewhere`; absent only when the app went to the back. Home
accepts it on `left` only, as a name from the app's code (identity invariant 34), and
stores it as sent; no migration, since the table keeps the body whole and has no
column per field.

The friction read counts, per place, the lefts that went to each screen (`nexts`),
and names the surfaces on which a left with a `next` was made by the window's start
(`nextsBefore`, one indexed read back per surface), so the report writer, which holds
the registry, says where a step was left from only over windows every build of that
surface could say it in (some-ui.friction/3, calls C1067-C1069).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LDpdUGw5QSYVRLeZJsw8D8
